        "ST-03": {"title": "Investigate nightly backtest import failure (Strategy Benchmark data-as-of line never populates)", "classification": "autonomous", "status": "done", "assigned_to": "engine", "github_issue": 1395, "branch": "exec/2026-08-14__release-v8.8/EPIC-01", "commit_sha": "ed06e996", "delegation_record_id": "DEL-20260814-01", "blocked_since_utc": null, "unblock_criteria": null, "completed_utc": "2026-08-14T19:30:00Z", "acceptance_verified": true, "spec_references": ["tests/test_strategy_benchmark_summary.py"], "spec_reference_not_applicable": true, "spec_reference_not_applicable_reason": "bug fix, no prior canonical spec governs get_backtest_summary()'s timestamp formatting — verified via tests/test_strategy_benchmark_summary.py and live production API confirmation.", "deviations_filed": true, "last_completed_substep": "3.1.A.push", "sign_off_record": null, "notes": "Reclassified delegated_backend -> autonomous (LL-v2.3-EX-02) — DEL-20260814-01 cancelled. Root cause: TIMESTAMPTZ value formatted with a naive-datetime-only 'append Z' pattern produced a malformed double-suffixed ISO string, parsed as Invalid Date by the frontend. AC-1 (backtest.yml run + imported_at) was already true pre-fix (confirmed via live GH Actions log for run 31766766669: 583 trades, correct imported_at). AC-2 (frontend line renders a recent date) fixed at the data layer; no frontend code changed, so the CLAUDE.md frontend-testing gate (Playwright/staging sign-off) does not apply to this story — recommend a quick post-deploy visual spot-check of the Strategy Benchmark page as a non-blocking confirmation, not a merge gate."},
